  "circulation": "Ranger, pavilion and bathhouse roofs act as landmarks. A central path and two signed loop trails keep the search bounded. Dock is a short visible terminal branch with no mandatory rite and no safe-water escape exploit.",
  "systems": "Rain runoff, creek audio, lake wind and ordinary campfire remnants have explicit baseline causes. Sheltered device-placement surfaces belong to actual deployed loadouts; no free equipment is scenery.",
  "campaign": "Guest ledger at ranger desk, mismatched trail markers and an abandoned camper account. Revisit exposes alternate interpretation of the same physical paths rather than inventing an unbuilt island.",
  "refine": [
    "Second remote exemplar: test shelter/calibration and tent visibility without foliage changing hiding geometry.",
    "Refine boardwalk/bridge supports, rails, lake collision and dock retreat timing.",
    "References and campground-specific sanitary/service construction still need measured review."
  ],
